 "result_text": "`git machete github checkout-pr` now says when a pull request is closed, instead of reporting it as not found. I checked that the module imports, but I haven't run the command or the tests.\n\nWhen the PR number isn't in the open-PR list, git-machete now makes one more GitHub API request for that single PR. If its state is `closed`, you get:\n\n```\nPR #204 is closed in repository `org/repo`\n```\n\nIf the follow-up request fails (a 404 for a PR that never existed, or an auth error), the old message stays: \"PR #204 is not found in repository `org/repo`\".\n\nI added a helper, `is_pull_request_closed`, in `git_machete/github.py` and call it from `checkout_github_prs` in `git_machete/client.py`. I didn't add or change any tests, and I didn't commit.",
